00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:12,960
 And I did CPR until the paramedics got there.

522
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:18,160
 And she went home to be with Jesus.

523
00:22:18,160 --> 00:22:23,920
 And that was a really discouraging, hard, brutal,

524
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:26,480
 painful period.

525
00:22:26,480 --> 00:22:30,000
 I knew she's in heaven, but I just missed her.

526
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:34,240
 She'd be 19 this year.

527
00:22:34,240 --> 00:22:40,440
 And everybody was so cool to me because they were like, dude,

528
00:22:40,440 --> 00:22:42,000
 your daughter just died.

529
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:43,920
 And I was cool to me because I was like, well,

530
00:22:43,920 --> 00:22:45,280
 my daughter just died.

531
00:22:45,280 --> 00:22:46,400
 I will have ice cream.

532
00:22:46,400 --> 00:22:47,480
 You know what I'm saying?

533
00:22:47,480 --> 00:22:52,080
 It's the ultimate diet hall pass.

534
00:22:52,080 --> 00:22:55,280
 I was so kind to myself in that season.

535
00:22:55,280 --> 00:22:58,520
 But here's the crazy thing about when

536
00:22:58,520 --> 00:23:03,520
 you feel like what made you you just got taken from you,

537
00:23:03,520 --> 00:23:05,800
 and you feel like you've lost your mind,

538
00:23:05,800 --> 00:23:06,880
 and you don't understand.

539
00:23:06,880 --> 00:23:09,520
 And there's not even a medical or explainable reason

540
00:23:09,520 --> 00:23:11,240
 as to why this is all happening.

541
00:23:11,240 --> 00:23:13,480
 That's what made that so confusing for me.

542
00:23:13,480 --> 00:23:15,800
 Because on paper, it was all fine.

543
00:23:15,800 --> 00:23:18,840
 And yet, it wasn't just the panic attacks.

544
00:23:18,840 --> 00:23:22,600
 It was also this weird feeling of dread

545
00:23:22,600 --> 00:23:24,960
 that I had never experienced in my life

546
00:23:24,960 --> 00:23:27,760
 before that was just constantly there pulling

547
00:23:27,760 --> 00:23:30,280
 at the edges of my lungs.

548
00:23:30,280 --> 00:23:33,720
 I've always felt gifted by the Holy Spirit

549
00:23:33,720 --> 00:23:40,280
 and just prone towards ideation, creativity, storytelling.

550
00:23:40,280 --> 00:23:43,040
 Here's what's next.

551
00:23:43,040 --> 00:23:47,160
 Where do you think Clover got it from, that type A.

552
00:23:47,160 --> 00:23:49,120
 And I felt like all of those things

553
00:23:49,120 --> 00:23:53,960
 that always were so natural, intuitive just got put in a bag

554
00:23:53,960 --> 00:23:55,720
 and taken away from me.

555
00:23:55,720 --> 00:24:00,080
 I, for the first time, had no sense of this is what's next.

556
00:24:00,080 --> 00:24:03,880
 And I was just like, how do I get that back?

557
00:24:03,880 --> 00:24:06,680
 Started to feel like I don't even--

558
00:24:06,680 --> 00:24:08,720
 have I gone as far as I can on my calling

559
00:24:08,720 --> 00:24:10,680
 and in the position I'm in?

560
00:24:10,680 --> 00:24:13,040
 Started to just-- all these big questions,

561
00:24:13,040 --> 00:24:15,400
 all these massive questions.

562
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:16,600
 So I go into the doctor.

563
00:24:16,600 --> 00:24:19,400
 I'm like, my testosterone level's fine.

564
00:24:19,400 --> 00:24:23,240
 Is there-- got scanned, got on paper.

565
00:24:23,240 --> 00:24:25,360
 None of this should be happening.

566
00:24:25,360 --> 00:24:27,940
 It didn't make any sense to me.

567
00:24:27,940 --> 00:24:32,240
 And it was a hard, difficult, discouraging season

568
00:24:32,240 --> 00:24:36,480
 to feel like I was lost in the woods

569
00:24:36,480 --> 00:24:39,000
 without a compass or any bearings,

570
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:40,440
 couldn't see the stars.

571
00:24:40,440 --> 00:24:44,200
 Would I ever get out of this?

572
00:24:44,200 --> 00:24:48,960
 I was reticent to call it what it was.

573
00:24:48,960 --> 00:24:50,600
 Some of you might have figured it out.

574
00:24:50,600 --> 00:24:51,560
 What was I having?

575
00:24:51,560 --> 00:24:57,160
 I was having a full-blown midlife crisis.

576
00:24:57,160 --> 00:24:59,320
 Oh, I would have hated it if you would have told me

577
00:24:59,320 --> 00:25:00,480
 that in the moment, though.

578
00:25:00,480 --> 00:25:03,200
 At any point in this 18-month-long journey,

579
00:25:03,200 --> 00:25:06,000
 had you insinuated to me, bro, this is-- chill.

580
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:06,760
 Take a breath.

581
00:25:06,760 --> 00:25:08,120
 You're having a midlife crisis.

582
00:25:08,120 --> 00:25:09,620
 I'd have been like, get out of here,

583
00:25:09,620 --> 00:25:11,200
 because that feels so cliche.

584
00:25:11,200 --> 00:25:12,400
 Like, what am I going to do?

585
00:25:12,400 --> 00:25:13,640
 Go buy a Corvette?

586
00:25:13,640 --> 00:25:16,160
 Unbutton my shirt to an uncomfortable degree?

587
00:25:16,160 --> 00:25:17,520
 Three more necklaces?

588
00:25:17,520 --> 00:25:19,320
 Like, get out of here, you know?

589
00:25:19,320 --> 00:25:20,320
 Start doing CrossFit?

590
00:25:20,320 --> 00:25:20,880
 I'm kidding.

591
00:25:20,880 --> 00:25:22,200
 I'm joking.

592
00:25:22,200 --> 00:25:23,360
 The classic midlife crisis.

593
00:25:23,360 --> 00:25:24,320
 Do an Ironman.

594
00:25:24,320 --> 00:25:28,320
 Just all the things, you know what I'm saying?

595
00:25:28,320 --> 00:25:34,640
 And yet, I was exactly in the halfway point

596
00:25:34,640 --> 00:25:37,520
 of the average life expectancy for a human being

597
00:25:37,520 --> 00:25:41,000
 on this planet, which, by the way, is 72.

598
00:25:41,000 --> 00:25:45,600
 72, globally, is the average amount

599
00:25:45,600 --> 00:25:47,640
 of time a human being gets to live

600
00:25:47,640 --> 00:25:50,920
 on this third rock from the sun.

601
00:25:50,920 --> 00:25:53,160
 So technically speaking, I was just a late bloomer.

602
00:25:53,160 --> 00:25:54,960
 I should have been having my midlife crisis

603
00:25:54,960 --> 00:25:59,560
 two years earlier, at 36, which is the halfway point of 72.

604
00:25:59,560 --> 00:26:01,640
 Here's something that'll really cook your noodle.

605
00:26:01,640 --> 00:26:04,680
 That means that 18 is the quarter life.

606
00:26:04,680 --> 00:26:07,000
 That's wild, right?

607
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:11,360
 And so I was spinning and having all this big, big questions

608
00:26:11,360 --> 00:26:14,200
 about purpose and mission and use of the time

609
00:26:14,200 --> 00:26:16,640
 that God gave me on this planet and all the rest.

610
00:26:16,640 --> 00:26:19,800
 And the big question was, how do I

611
00:26:19,800 --> 00:26:25,360
 regain my footing to find my way through my calling with joy?

612
00:26:25,360 --> 00:26:29,560
 Again, knowing all of the points to Jonathan Edwards' sermon

613
00:26:29,560 --> 00:26:32,640
 didn't keep me from feeling discouraged in that moment.

614
00:26:32,640 --> 00:26:34,720
 Now, just to pause and bring us all in here,

615
00:26:34,720 --> 00:26:36,600
 because some of you might be like, well, hey,

616
00:26:36,600 --> 00:26:37,520
 that's great, Boomer.

617
00:26:37,520 --> 00:26:41,840
 I'll call you if I need you when I get there.

618
00:26:41,840 --> 00:26:43,880
 But here's the reality.

619
00:26:43,880 --> 00:26:46,280
 It's not just people in midlife who

620
00:26:46,280 --> 00:26:48,800
 end up facing crisis like this.

621
00:26:48,800 --> 00:26:51,440
 In fact, as I've now looked into it and written on it

622
00:26:51,440 --> 00:26:54,760
 and spent in the last several years bottling up

623
00:26:54,760 --> 00:26:57,360
 some of these lessons and distilling them to try

624
00:26:57,360 --> 00:27:01,200
 and help other people-- because I believe anything you fight

625
00:27:01,200 --> 00:27:03,880
 your way through, you should turn back and generously help

626
00:27:03,880 --> 00:27:05,340
 whoever's coming behind you, right?

627
00:27:05,340 --> 00:27:07,960
 That's biblical, to give comfort you've received.

628
00:27:07,960 --> 00:27:11,080
 And what I've discovered is that midlife

629
00:27:11,080 --> 00:27:13,760
 isn't the only kind of crisis that people

630
00:27:13,760 --> 00:27:14,760
 face in this world.

631
00:27:14,760 --> 00:27:16,800
 In fact, it's not even the most common.

632
00:27:16,800 --> 00:27:19,040
 Did you know that later life crisis is

633
00:27:19,040 --> 00:27:21,040
 far more common than midlife?

634
00:27:21,040 --> 00:27:23,840
 And that's defined as those retirement years,

635
00:27:23,840 --> 00:27:25,240
 the empty nest era.

636
00:27:25,240 --> 00:27:27,280
 For some of you, be kind to your folks.

637
00:27:27,280 --> 00:27:29,820
 What they're walking through is uncharted territory for them.

638
00:27:29,820 --> 00:27:33,760
 They spent the last 18 years of their lives serving and caring

639
00:27:33,760 --> 00:27:35,320
 and being there for you.

640
00:27:35,320 --> 00:27:36,740
 And so they're finding their way--

641
00:27:36,740 --> 00:27:38,620
 you might be like, oh, they don't understand.

642
00:27:38,620 --> 00:27:39,960
 They don't understand themselves.

643
00:27:39,960 --> 00:27:41,720
 What they're going through is uncharted for them,

644
00:27:41,720 --> 00:27:43,600
 just like it's uncharted for you to be going through what

645
00:27:43,600 --> 00:27:44,760
 you're going through.

646
00:27:44,760 --> 00:27:47,320
 But did you know that currently-- this is 2026

647
00:27:47,320 --> 00:27:47,960
 data--

648
00:27:47,960 --> 00:27:52,020
 the most common kind of crisis you can go through in America

649
00:27:52,020 --> 00:27:55,800
 today is actually not the later life nor the midlife.

650
00:27:55,800 --> 00:27:58,320
 It's currently what they are calling the quarter life

651
00:27:58,320 --> 00:27:59,280
 crisis.

652
00:27:59,280 --> 00:28:02,440
 And it is the exact demographic that's

653
00:28:02,440 --> 00:28:06,840
 eligible to come here to the porch, that 18 to 30-ish kind

654
00:28:06,840 --> 00:28:10,080
 of like loosey-goosey phase, where there's just like,

655
00:28:10,080 --> 00:28:11,280
 I'm not in high school.

656
00:28:11,280 --> 00:28:12,680
 I'm not even in college anymore.

657
00:28:12,680 --> 00:28:15,220
 Like, the career, the life, laundry bills.

658
00:28:15,220 --> 00:28:18,120
 Like, is there a job for me with AI encroaching?

659
00:28:18,120 --> 00:28:20,640
 Like, all of this, this big stuff

660
00:28:20,640 --> 00:28:22,600
 that's being pushed upon you.

661
00:28:22,600 --> 00:28:25,120
 And I think a lot of times, we can just feel like we're not

662
00:28:25,120 --> 00:28:27,760
 equipped for the season of life that we're in.

663
00:28:27,760 --> 00:28:31,120
 That no one prepared us for what we're having to deal with here.

664
00:28:31,120 --> 00:28:34,640
 That we're an imposter in the story that is our life.

665
00:28:34,640 --> 00:28:37,360
 And just this feeling of like, I feel behind.

666
00:28:37,360 --> 00:28:40,400
 Like, I've got friends who are closing in on 40,

667
00:28:40,400 --> 00:28:41,360
 and they're not married.

668
00:28:41,360 --> 00:28:42,320
 They feel like, I'm behind.

669
00:28:42,320 --> 00:28:43,240
 I don't have kids yet.

670
00:28:43,240 --> 00:28:44,600
 If I am married, I feel behind.

671
00:28:44,600 --> 00:28:46,240
 I should be further along in my career.

672
00:28:46,240 --> 00:28:47,600
 I feel behind.

673
00:28:47,600 --> 00:28:53,160
 Or I'm exactly where I want to be in my calling,

674
00:28:53,160 --> 00:28:54,720
 or my career, or my family, but it

675
00:28:54,720 --> 00:28:57,680
 doesn't feel like I thought it would feel.

676
00:28:57,680 --> 00:28:59,420
 I was talking to someone the other day

677
00:28:59,420 --> 00:29:02,280
 who told me that they sold a company they built, scaled,

678
00:29:02,280 --> 00:29:04,240
 and always intended to sell.

679
00:29:04,240 --> 00:29:05,920
 And they knew God called them to do it.

680
00:29:05,920 --> 00:29:06,920
 They knew God led them.

681
00:29:06,920 --> 00:29:07,840
 They knew God provided.

682
00:29:07,840 --> 00:29:08,520
 They weren't stupid.

683
00:29:08,520 --> 00:29:09,960
 They were not turning into an idol

684
00:29:09,960 --> 00:29:11,080
 they're giving them glory for.

685
00:29:11,080 --> 00:29:13,200
 But they said the day they got to that finish line

686
00:29:13,200 --> 00:29:15,960
 and sold it was the emptiest and most discouraged

687
00:29:15,960 --> 00:29:17,620
 they ever felt.

688
00:29:17,620 --> 00:29:19,960
 Because it was what they knew they were supposed to do,

689
00:29:19,960 --> 00:29:20,960
 but when they got to it, it didn't

690
00:29:20,960 --> 00:29:22,800
 feel like they thought it was going to feel.

691
00:29:22,800 --> 00:29:25,680
 I think for a lot of us, whatever the finish line--

692
00:29:25,680 --> 00:29:27,240
 and I'm not talking about ego stuff,

693
00:29:27,240 --> 00:29:28,880
 and I'm not talking about pride stuff.

694
00:29:28,880 --> 00:29:31,120
 I'm talking about stuff we know God's called us to do.

695
00:29:31,120 --> 00:29:33,160
 When we get to those finish lines,

696
00:29:33,160 --> 00:29:36,000
 they just don't feel like we thought

697
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:38,160
 they were going to feel.

698
00:29:38,160 --> 00:29:42,920
 So for whatever reason, we can end up spiraling.

699
00:29:42,920 --> 00:29:47,000
 But what God began to show me, what Hebrews 12, 11 is saying,

700
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:49,600
 is that for every one of us losing heart going,

701
00:29:49,600 --> 00:29:53,040
 now where is this that God's got in?

702
00:29:53,040 --> 00:29:59,840
 Oh, waiting for you to erupt in your spirit with a wow, wow,

703
00:29:59,840 --> 00:30:00,360
 wow.

704
00:30:00,360 --> 00:30:02,880
 I see what you had in store.

705
00:30:02,880 --> 00:30:04,340
 There is a payoff.

706
00:30:04,340 --> 00:30:05,440
 There is a peace.

707
00:30:05,440 --> 00:30:07,360
 There is a godliness boost.

708
00:30:07,360 --> 00:30:08,720
 There is something inside.

709
00:30:08,720 --> 00:30:11,480
 If we don't lose heart, there is, I believe,

710
00:30:11,480 --> 00:30:16,960
 blessing waiting for us in our seasons of spiraling.

711
00:30:16,960 --> 00:30:20,680
 Blessed are the poor in spirit. Blessed are those who mourn.

712
00:30:20,680 --> 00:30:22,040
 Blessed are those who grieve.

713
00:30:22,040 --> 00:30:24,920
 None of us want to be any of those things, by the way.

714
00:30:24,920 --> 00:30:28,400
 Give me the choice of being poor in spirit or rich in faith.

715
00:30:28,400 --> 00:30:29,520
 I'm picking rich in faith.

716
00:30:29,520 --> 00:30:31,600
 Anybody with me?

717
00:30:31,600 --> 00:30:34,560
 Blessed are those who mourn.

718
00:30:34,560 --> 00:30:38,440
 Part of me wants to interrupt Jesus giving the beatitudes.

719
00:30:38,440 --> 00:30:39,760
 Time out.

720
00:30:39,760 --> 00:30:41,240
 No one's blessed for mourning.

721
00:30:41,240 --> 00:30:43,440
 Mourning sucks.

722
00:30:43,440 --> 00:30:46,060
 Grieving is awful.

723
00:30:46,060 --> 00:30:47,600
 It's terrible.

724
00:30:47,600 --> 00:30:50,560
 And yet Jesus is saying, there's actually favor on you

725
00:30:50,560 --> 00:30:53,040
 in the midst of these hard things.

726
00:30:53,040 --> 00:30:55,400
 You're going, what are you talking-- what are you smoking?

727
00:30:55,400 --> 00:30:56,280
 Get out of here.

728
00:30:56,280 --> 00:30:57,080
 Just go.

729
00:30:57,080 --> 00:30:59,360
 Go back to Montana immediately.

730
00:30:59,360 --> 00:31:01,520
 Go peddle that nonsense somewhere else.

731
00:31:01,520 --> 00:31:04,160
 What's the blessing waiting for us in our spiraling?

732
00:31:04,160 --> 00:31:10,880
 Listen, I understand spiraling's awful, debilitating, confusing,

733
00:31:10,880 --> 00:31:11,880
 destabilizing.

734
00:31:11,880 --> 00:31:14,440
 And yet I could pass five polygraphs

735
00:31:14,440 --> 00:31:16,260
 with the light of Jesus shining in my eyes

736
00:31:16,260 --> 00:31:18,360
 to tell you there is blessing for you

737
00:31:18,360 --> 00:31:20,800
 in the midst of your difficulty.

738
00:31:20,800 --> 00:31:24,840
 And this specific 18-month-long season of my life

739
00:31:24,840 --> 00:31:28,840
 that I was walking through from 38 to 40, I look back on now,

740
00:31:28,840 --> 00:31:31,340
 and I am so grateful for those hard nights.

741
00:31:31,340 --> 00:31:33,260
 I am so grateful not just for the nights where

742
00:31:33,260 --> 00:31:35,000
 there was a panic attack, but the next night where

743
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:36,400
 I was wondering with the tremors,

744
00:31:36,400 --> 00:31:37,520
 is it going to happen again?

745
00:31:37,520 --> 00:31:42,040
 I'm so grateful for what?

746
00:31:42,040 --> 00:31:48,200
 The way that God came near, the way that God right-sized me.

747
00:31:48,200 --> 00:31:49,620
 Listen, when we're cruising along

748
00:31:49,620 --> 00:31:51,240
 and we're catching all the green lights

749
00:31:51,240 --> 00:31:53,160
 and we just feel like everything that God has

750
00:31:53,160 --> 00:31:55,800
 is touching turns to gold, there can be a way

751
00:31:55,800 --> 00:31:58,800
 that you become bigger in your life than God.

752
00:31:58,800 --> 00:32:00,920
 And in these hard moments, these difficult moments

753
00:32:00,920 --> 00:32:02,920
 when we're crying out to him like we

754
00:32:02,920 --> 00:32:05,560
 should be all the time for our next breath,

755
00:32:05,560 --> 00:32:08,520
 that God shows up in our story in the way

756
00:32:08,520 --> 00:32:11,960
 that we only can when he is literally giving us

757
00:32:11,960 --> 00:32:13,200
 our next breath.

758
00:32:13,200 --> 00:32:14,080
 And God is there.

759
00:32:14,080 --> 00:32:17,200
 I speak over your 2 AM fear.

760
00:32:17,200 --> 00:32:19,640
 I speak over your anxiousness.

761
00:32:19,640 --> 00:32:22,880
 I speak over your loneliness and the sense of,

762
00:32:22,880 --> 00:32:25,120
 like, am I going to make it through this, that God

763
00:32:25,120 --> 00:32:28,560
 is seeking to meet you in these moments in ways

764
00:32:28,560 --> 00:32:29,720
 that you could never expect.

765
00:32:29,720 --> 00:32:32,920
 He's near to the brokenhearted.

766
00:32:32,920 --> 00:32:37,200
 He saves such as have a contrite spirit.

767
00:32:37,200 --> 00:32:42,800
 There is blessing for you in your seasons of spiraling.

768
00:32:42,800 --> 00:32:46,680
 When we took all of these truths and began

769
00:32:46,680 --> 00:32:50,520
 to feel a calling to put them in a book and release it, why?

770
00:32:50,520 --> 00:32:53,320
 Because books have changed my life.

771
00:32:53,320 --> 00:32:56,520
 And I wanted to continue to offer up to anybody coming

772
00:32:56,520 --> 00:32:58,800
 behind me who feels like they're going through something

773
00:32:58,800 --> 00:33:00,640
 they're not going to make it through.

774
00:33:00,640 --> 00:33:03,080
 We began to feel like we should put this into a book.

775
00:33:03,080 --> 00:33:05,040
 I told the publisher, I just asked

776
00:33:05,040 --> 00:33:07,640
 that you put on the cover a tornado built out

777
00:33:07,640 --> 00:33:09,280
 of wildflowers.

778
00:33:09,280 --> 00:33:10,240
 Why?

779
00:33:10,240 --> 00:33:13,800
 Why tornado specifically built out of wildflowers?

780
00:33:13,800 --> 00:33:15,960
 Because the tornado is one of nature's

781
00:33:15,960 --> 00:33:18,560
 most destructive symbols.

782
00:33:18,560 --> 00:33:20,920
 A tornado coming on the horizon will tear a house down,

783
00:33:20,920 --> 00:33:22,160
 will tear a neighborhood down.

784
00:33:22,160 --> 00:33:26,640
 And yet, the juxtaposition of, yes, it's your mourning,

785
00:33:26,640 --> 00:33:29,640
 you're grieving, you're hurting, you're confused.

786
00:33:29,640 --> 00:33:35,160
 And yet, the poetry, the beauty, the art of this tornado

787
00:33:35,160 --> 00:33:38,600
 being built out of flowers, that was the image in my heart,

788
00:33:38,600 --> 00:33:43,280
 in my life, as I began to feel like God was growing me

789
00:33:43,280 --> 00:33:44,680
 in the spiral.

790
00:33:44,680 --> 00:33:47,080
 He was deepening me.

791
00:33:47,080 --> 00:33:51,120
 I was encountering Him in the spiral, that He came near,

792
00:33:51,120 --> 00:33:53,680
 that I was humbled, that I was right sized,

793
00:33:53,680 --> 00:33:58,440
 that I began to feel like Isaiah chapter 6.

794
00:33:58,440 --> 00:34:02,760
 Like in the year King Uzziah died, I saw the Lord.

795
00:34:02,760 --> 00:34:04,960
 Do you see the juxtaposition there?

796
00:34:04,960 --> 00:34:06,640
 I'm spiraling low.

797
00:34:06,640 --> 00:34:08,240
 This king that I loved was taken out.

798
00:34:08,240 --> 00:34:10,240
 And yet, there I saw the Lord on His throne.

799
00:34:10,240 --> 00:34:11,040
 That's the beauty.

800
00:34:11,040 --> 00:34:14,480
 That's the tornado, but it's built out of wildflowers.

801
00:34:14,480 --> 00:34:16,360
 Holy, holy, holy, out of what?

802
00:34:16,360 --> 00:34:20,000
 Woe is me, I am undone.

803
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:23,680
 The way that God produces in you what He can then take you

804
00:34:23,680 --> 00:34:25,400
 to the next level with.

805
00:34:25,400 --> 00:34:28,080
 The way God prepares you.

806
00:34:28,080 --> 00:34:33,160
 It was A.W. Tozer who said that it is doubtful that God can use

807
00:34:33,160 --> 00:34:38,640
 a person greatly until He has first bruised them deeply.

808
00:34:38,640 --> 00:34:41,800
 If we can choose to speak over, and speak about,

809
00:34:41,800 --> 00:34:45,760
 and think about, and look at our seasons of spiraling

810
00:34:45,760 --> 00:34:49,360
 and difficulty as God getting ready, as God preparing,

811
00:34:49,360 --> 00:34:54,360
 as God choosing to honor us enough,

812
00:34:54,360 --> 00:34:57,280
 to entrust us with a trial that can hone and shape

813
00:34:57,280 --> 00:35:00,680
 the edge of our soul for what He wants to do with us next.

814
00:35:00,680 --> 00:35:04,240
 If we could actually believe a season of spiraling

815
00:35:04,240 --> 00:35:07,240
 is God's great compliment upon us,

816
00:35:07,240 --> 00:35:09,640
 that He wants to come near to us and come close to us

817
00:35:09,640 --> 00:35:11,440
 in that unique and particular way.

818
00:35:11,440 --> 00:35:14,040
 It was Charles Spurgeon who said that God gives

819
00:35:14,040 --> 00:35:20,240
 His most difficult assignments to His most trusted soldiers.

820
00:35:20,240 --> 00:35:21,840
 Because here's the reality.

821
00:35:21,840 --> 00:35:25,280
 All of us have a misconception--

822
00:35:25,280 --> 00:35:28,360
 I've done it so many times in my life-- of what we think

823
00:35:28,360 --> 00:35:30,640
 growth can and should look like.

824
00:35:30,640 --> 00:35:32,880
 Here's what we want growth to look like.

825
00:35:32,880 --> 00:35:36,600
 Just up and to the right indefinitely.

826
00:35:36,600 --> 00:35:39,520
 A vertical line so steep you could ski down this sucker.

827
00:35:39,520 --> 00:35:41,400
 This is what I want my marriage to look like.

828
00:35:41,400 --> 00:35:44,200
 This is what I want my growth and Christ-likeness

829
00:35:44,200 --> 00:35:44,800
 to look like.

830
00:35:44,800 --> 00:35:47,120
 This is what I want my ministry to look like.

831
00:35:47,120 --> 00:35:48,440
 Just up and to the right forever.

832
00:35:48,440 --> 00:35:51,640
 But that's not realistic or desirable.

833
00:35:51,640 --> 00:35:54,920
 A better picture my counselor helped me to see and understand

834
00:35:54,920 --> 00:35:58,040
 was that this is what true growth looks like.

835
00:35:58,040 --> 00:35:59,440
 It's more unpredictable.

836
00:35:59,440 --> 00:36:00,360
 It's more broken.

837
00:36:00,360 --> 00:36:01,240
 It's more janky.

838
00:36:01,240 --> 00:36:03,000
 It's a little bit, and then over,

839
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:04,480
 and then you plateau in that growth,

840
00:36:04,480 --> 00:36:06,240
 and then you take a new break.

841
00:36:06,240 --> 00:36:11,120
 What he said to me is growth is not like a straight line.

842
00:36:11,120 --> 00:36:12,120
 It's actually like what?

843
00:36:12,120 --> 00:36:13,580
 What does that actually look like?

844
00:36:13,580 --> 00:36:15,880
 Stairs.

845
00:36:15,880 --> 00:36:19,000
 And what that means, then, is that whenever

846
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:21,320
 you've come to the end of a growth

847
00:36:21,320 --> 00:36:23,160
 mode in your character, in your development,

848
00:36:23,160 --> 00:36:25,040
 in your calling, in your relationship,

849
00:36:25,040 --> 00:36:26,320
 you first hit what?

850
00:36:26,320 --> 00:36:28,800
 You hit a wall.

851
00:36:28,800 --> 00:36:31,040
 But what if what you hit-- what if what

852
00:36:31,040 --> 00:36:33,900
 I felt like I hit at 60 miles an hour wasn't a wall?

853
00:36:33,900 --> 00:36:35,520
 What if it was a stair?

854
00:36:35,520 --> 00:36:37,000
 What if it was the opportunity?

855
00:36:37,000 --> 00:36:38,840
 What if it was the cue to grow?

856
00:36:38,840 --> 00:36:41,600
 What if it was now the chance to take a step of trust?

857
00:36:41,600 --> 00:36:44,360
 To take a step into the wilderness with God?

858
00:36:44,360 --> 00:36:46,600
 To have everything torn back.

859
00:36:46,600 --> 00:36:48,000
 To get back to brass tacks.

860
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:49,240
 To come to know Him.

861
00:36:49,240 --> 00:36:51,800
 To have Him become all I need, because in that moment,

862
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:54,360
 He's all I have.

863
00:36:54,360 --> 00:36:57,360
 And so what that means to you is that you

864
00:36:57,360 --> 00:37:01,120
 can begin to use different language to speak

865
00:37:01,120 --> 00:37:03,440
 about your seasons of suffering.

866
00:37:03,440 --> 00:37:05,720
 These dark nights of the soul.

867
00:37:05,720 --> 00:37:09,040
 What if instead of having the fatalistic, bleak language

868
00:37:09,040 --> 00:37:14,040
 of I'm cooked, we're toast, this is over, we're done.

869
00:37:14,040 --> 00:37:15,920
 It's never going to get better.

870
00:37:15,920 --> 00:37:16,960
 I'm being destroyed.

871
00:37:16,960 --> 00:37:20,520
 What if instead you could say, I'm being deepened.

872
00:37:20,520 --> 00:37:22,560
 I'm being developed.

873
00:37:22,560 --> 00:37:26,880
 I went as far as I could with the tools

874
00:37:26,880 --> 00:37:29,200
 I currently possessed.

875
00:37:29,200 --> 00:37:32,460
 But God is bringing me into a desert place.

876
00:37:32,460 --> 00:37:34,160
 He's bringing me into a wilderness place.

877
00:37:34,160 --> 00:37:36,800
 He's bringing me into a wilderness place

878
00:37:36,800 --> 00:37:41,480
 to retool me for what He has next for me.

879
00:37:41,480 --> 00:37:44,280
 I love this company, Shinola.

880
00:37:44,280 --> 00:37:45,600
 It's a watch company.

881
00:37:45,600 --> 00:37:47,480
 How they make turntables, and bicycles,

882
00:37:47,480 --> 00:37:48,760
 and all kinds of random stuff.

883
00:37:48,760 --> 00:37:50,840
 They make them all in Detroit.

884
00:37:50,840 --> 00:37:52,560
 And what they've done is they've taken

885
00:37:52,560 --> 00:37:55,280
 some of these auto manufacturing facilities

886
00:37:55,280 --> 00:37:58,440
 where production ended up going over and out.

887
00:37:58,440 --> 00:38:01,520
 And we know Detroit, the city, in a lot of ways,

888
00:38:01,520 --> 00:38:04,160
 like some of its glory days were kind of behind it.

889
00:38:04,160 --> 00:38:07,480
 And this company has chosen to take some of these buildings

890
00:38:07,480 --> 00:38:09,000
 that are no longer making cars.

891
00:38:09,000 --> 00:38:10,040
 And people don't have to.

892
00:38:10,040 --> 00:38:13,240
 And now they're bringing beauty, and these artistry items out

893
00:38:13,240 --> 00:38:15,360
 of it, watches, and bicycles, and turntables,

894
00:38:15,360 --> 00:38:16,240
 and all this stuff.

895
00:38:16,240 --> 00:38:20,720
 And I love the thought that these factories didn't

896
00:38:20,720 --> 00:38:22,480
 need to be torn down.

897
00:38:22,480 --> 00:38:26,280
 They just needed to be retooled to make what is new,

898
00:38:26,280 --> 00:38:28,860
 to make what is current, to make something bespoke, to make

899
00:38:28,860 --> 00:38:29,720
 something beautiful.

900
00:38:29,720 --> 00:38:31,820
 In your life, whenever you feel like, oh my gosh,

901
00:38:31,820 --> 00:38:33,080
 there's nothing more for me.

902
00:38:33,080 --> 00:38:34,080
 No, no, listen.

903
00:38:34,080 --> 00:38:35,960
 This doesn't need to be torn down.

904
00:38:35,960 --> 00:38:38,720
 Just retooled that God's preparing you

905
00:38:38,720 --> 00:38:42,160
 for what He has prepared you for.

906
00:38:42,160 --> 00:38:45,920
 That there's a blessing for you in your spiraling.

907
00:38:45,920 --> 00:38:48,800
 Many of us read in the news and saw on Instagram

908
00:38:48,800 --> 00:38:51,200
 all the story about Jeremy Renner, the actor who

909
00:38:51,200 --> 00:38:53,600
 plays Hawkeye, among other things.

910
00:38:53,600 --> 00:38:59,640
 He got accidentally run over by his own 14,000 pound snowplow

911
00:38:59,640 --> 00:39:02,880
 while trying to save the life of his nephew.

912
00:39:02,880 --> 00:39:07,160
 Broke 30 bones, pierced his lungs, crushed his skull.

913
00:39:07,160 --> 00:39:09,760
 Should not have lived.

914
00:39:09,760 --> 00:39:11,440
 But I was listening to an interview

915
00:39:11,440 --> 00:39:14,640
 where he was asked, like, are you better yet?

916
00:39:14,640 --> 00:39:16,600
 Are you back yet?

917
00:39:16,600 --> 00:39:18,200
 Do you feel like you've recovered yet?

918
00:39:18,200 --> 00:39:20,060
 And he said, no.

919
00:39:20,060 --> 00:39:22,360
 The guy said, I don't think you understood the question.

920
00:39:22,360 --> 00:39:24,360
 I'm asking, like, do you feel like you're back to where

921
00:39:24,360 --> 00:39:25,640
 you were before the accident?

922
00:39:25,640 --> 00:39:27,680
 He goes, no, I'm not back.

923
00:39:27,680 --> 00:39:30,720
 I'm better.

924
00:39:30,720 --> 00:39:34,760
 He then said, I got so many gifts from almost dying.

925
00:39:34,760 --> 00:39:37,800
 I'm not back.

926
00:39:37,800 --> 00:39:39,360
 I'm better.

927
00:39:39,360 --> 00:39:41,320
 But God stripped me down.

928
00:39:41,320 --> 00:39:43,200
 God had me lying down.

929
00:39:43,200 --> 00:39:45,440
 God had me at the place where I literally

930
00:39:45,440 --> 00:39:47,640
 did not think I was going to make it through this.

931
00:39:47,640 --> 00:39:48,140
 Why?

932
00:39:48,140 --> 00:39:51,400
 To give you so many gifts from dying.

933
00:39:51,400 --> 00:39:54,280
 Tim Keller once said, Christianity

934
00:39:54,280 --> 00:39:57,800
 is not about going from strength to strength and just grace

935
00:39:57,800 --> 00:39:58,520
 to grace.

936
00:39:58,520 --> 00:40:01,760
 It's a religion predicated upon going from death

937
00:40:01,760 --> 00:40:03,120
 to resurrection.

938
00:40:03,120 --> 00:40:06,280
 And as he did it, he's doing it in you.

939
00:40:06,280 --> 00:40:09,640
 When you feel like you've been brought to a place of death,

940
00:40:09,640 --> 00:40:13,440
 let me tell you, there's resurrection that can follow,

941
00:40:13,440 --> 00:40:17,600
 because you're filled with the same Holy Spirit that raised

942
00:40:17,600 --> 00:40:20,520
 Christ Jesus from the dead.

943
00:40:20,520 --> 00:40:22,800
 You remember that when you feel like it's over.

944
00:40:22,800 --> 00:40:24,940
 You remember that when you feel like your greatest days were

945
00:40:24,940 --> 00:40:25,440
 behind.

946
00:40:25,440 --> 00:40:28,120
 You feel like when you feel like there's nothing more for you.

947
00:40:28,120 --> 00:40:29,360
 There's no point for you.

948
00:40:29,360 --> 00:40:34,320
 You are about to go from death in Jesus' name to resurrection.

949
00:40:34,320 --> 00:40:36,200
 He's got something more for your future.

950
00:40:36,200 --> 00:40:38,640
 If you're not dead, he's not done.

951
00:40:38,640 --> 00:40:43,280
 He's still with you, so take a shaky step in his name.

952
00:40:43,280 --> 00:40:47,220
 Up that jagged staircase of growth,

953
00:40:47,220 --> 00:40:50,320
 there's blessing for you in your spiraling.

954
00:40:50,320 --> 00:40:53,760
 Is that not what James is saying when he says in James 1,

955
00:40:53,760 --> 00:40:57,840
 verse 2, "Consider it pure joy, my brethren,

956
00:40:57,840 --> 00:41:01,000
 when you face various trials of all these different kinds?"

957
00:41:01,000 --> 00:41:01,480
 Why?

958
00:41:01,480 --> 00:41:04,440
 Because you know that the testing of your faith

959
00:41:04,440 --> 00:41:05,880
 develops perseverance.

960
00:41:05,880 --> 00:41:07,480
 Think about that as a step.

961
00:41:07,480 --> 00:41:09,760
 And from there, God wants to develop your perseverance

962
00:41:09,760 --> 00:41:14,500
 into finishing its work so that you may be mature and complete,

963
00:41:14,500 --> 00:41:17,360
 lacking nothing.

964
00:41:17,360 --> 00:41:19,960
 There's a-- and I love it because we don't even

965
00:41:19,960 --> 00:41:22,840
 have to imagine as we think about a staircase and a spiral

966
00:41:22,840 --> 00:41:26,720
 because literally it's climbing a spiral staircase.

967
00:41:26,720 --> 00:41:32,080
 It is a symbol that we have a mental picture for of how we--

968
00:41:32,080 --> 00:41:33,880
 what that means, though, is that we

969
00:41:33,880 --> 00:41:37,520
 have to stop thinking about spiraling down

970
00:41:37,520 --> 00:41:39,880
 like a graveyard spiral a plane would enter,

971
00:41:39,880 --> 00:41:44,320
 and we have to choose in Jesus' name to spiral up,

972
00:41:44,320 --> 00:41:45,840
 to spiral in the right direction.

973
00:41:45,840 --> 00:41:46,320
 Why?

974
00:41:46,320 --> 00:41:48,760
 Because we are in an upside-down kingdom.

975
00:41:48,760 --> 00:41:50,980
 So even though we feel like we're being struck down

976
00:41:50,980 --> 00:41:54,240
 and hard-pressed and discouraged, what's happening?

977
00:41:54,240 --> 00:41:58,040
 He's showing the life of Christ, the divine life of Christ,

978
00:41:58,040 --> 00:41:59,960
 who gives you all things pertaining to life

979
00:41:59,960 --> 00:42:02,480
 and godliness, is at work in you.

980
00:42:02,480 --> 00:42:05,040
 And when Paul got so discouraged in 2 Corinthians 1

981
00:42:05,040 --> 00:42:07,520
 that he despaired even of life itself, what did he say?

982
00:42:07,520 --> 00:42:10,720
 He said, these things happen to me

983
00:42:10,720 --> 00:42:13,960
 so that I would not trust in myself,

984
00:42:13,960 --> 00:42:16,920
 but so that I would trust in God who raises the dead.

985
00:42:16,920 --> 00:42:19,960
 When you come to a season of spiraling, listen to me,

986
00:42:19,960 --> 00:42:24,160
 God allowed it to happen so you would not trust in yourself,

987
00:42:24,160 --> 00:42:26,880
 but you would trust in whatever crisis you're in,

988
00:42:26,880 --> 00:42:29,840
 in the God who raises the dead.

989
00:42:29,840 --> 00:42:31,600
 So I believe in Jesus' name.

990
00:42:31,600 --> 00:42:34,840
 There's a wow, wow, wow coming for you

991
00:42:34,840 --> 00:42:40,400
 if you would just be willing to put the label-maker down

992
00:42:40,400 --> 00:42:43,780
 and stop trying to label things before he's finished.

993
00:42:43,780 --> 00:42:45,240
 Because you're going to call it bad.

994
00:42:45,240 --> 00:42:46,880
 You're going to call it terrible, losing that job

995
00:42:46,880 --> 00:42:48,160
 and having that person betray you

996
00:42:48,160 --> 00:42:50,260
 and going through what you're going to go through.

997
00:42:50,260 --> 00:42:51,440
 And that medical emergency, you're

998
00:42:51,440 --> 00:42:53,400
 going to want to say, this is bad, this is bad.

999
00:42:53,400 --> 00:42:56,240
 And how crazy would it be for us to be labeling something

1000
00:42:56,240 --> 00:42:59,000
 bad that God already has in his mind determined

1001
00:42:59,000 --> 00:43:02,080
 from before the foundation of the world that he's

1002
00:43:02,080 --> 00:43:07,520
 going to use to bring forth good for you and glory for him.

1003
00:43:07,520 --> 00:43:10,020
 And that the day could come that you would look back upon it

1004
00:43:10,020 --> 00:43:13,260
 as one of the most treasured things you ever experienced,

1005
00:43:13,260 --> 00:43:15,960
 but you were tempted in a moment to label it

1006
00:43:15,960 --> 00:43:18,520
 like you knew better than him.

1007
00:43:18,520 --> 00:43:22,760
 So with all due respect, put the label-maker down.

1008
00:43:22,760 --> 00:43:25,800
 If you hear me and you've received, hopefully,

1009
00:43:25,800 --> 00:43:29,400
 some encouragement that could help you navigate future

1010
00:43:29,400 --> 00:43:32,120
 spiraling, I praise God for that.

1011
00:43:32,120 --> 00:43:35,080
 But I wonder if maybe there's one or two here today

1012
00:43:35,080 --> 00:43:38,280
 who would say, man, I'm spiraling right now.

1013
00:43:38,280 --> 00:43:40,040
 This isn't some future hypothetical.

1014
00:43:40,040 --> 00:43:43,120
 I'm spiraling literally today.

1015
00:43:43,120 --> 00:43:45,740
 What do I need to do right now in a moment of spiraling?

1016
00:43:45,740 --> 00:43:48,120
 I'm going to give it to you, and you could jot these down.

1017
00:43:48,120 --> 00:43:51,120
 Five quick things that are going to be done that hopefully

1018
00:43:51,120 --> 00:43:52,600
 would be helpful to you.

1019
00:43:52,600 --> 00:43:56,960
 Or, here we go, for someone you care about who

1020
00:43:56,960 --> 00:43:58,120
 you're watching spiraling.

1021
00:43:58,120 --> 00:44:00,560
 My wife Jenny is the unsung hero in all of this

1022
00:44:00,560 --> 00:44:02,600
 because she was right there with me.

1023
00:44:02,600 --> 00:44:04,760
 And secondhand spiraling is real.

1024
00:44:04,760 --> 00:44:07,300
 To know how to care for someone in chaos

1025
00:44:07,300 --> 00:44:09,000
 without falling into crisis yourself

1026
00:44:09,000 --> 00:44:13,560
 is an art to be celebrated and a calling to be recognized.

1027
00:44:13,560 --> 00:44:15,760
 So this could be for you or for a friend or someone

1028
00:44:15,760 --> 00:44:17,520
 you love who is spiraling today.

1029
00:44:17,520 --> 00:44:19,240
 Five things to do when you're spiraling.

1030
00:44:19,240 --> 00:44:22,360
 Number one, understand the season you're in

1031
00:44:22,360 --> 00:44:24,880
 and the one you're heading into.

1032
00:44:24,880 --> 00:44:27,960
 Think about the season you're in today

1033
00:44:27,960 --> 00:44:29,280
 and the one that's coming next.

1034
00:44:29,280 --> 00:44:30,040
 This can help you.

1035
00:44:30,040 --> 00:44:31,160
 This is what the Bible says.

1036
00:44:31,160 --> 00:44:36,600
 Help me to know a day is coming when I'm going to die.

1037
00:44:36,600 --> 00:44:38,200
 This will give me a heart of wisdom.

1038
00:44:38,200 --> 00:44:39,600
 That's what David said, right?

1039
00:44:39,600 --> 00:44:40,880
 Help me to consider my end.

1040
00:44:40,880 --> 00:44:44,120
 Help me to remember my days are not infinite but finite.

1041
00:44:44,120 --> 00:44:47,720
 The 72-year thing, when you think about that,

1042
00:44:47,720 --> 00:44:49,280
 it will give you a heart of wisdom.

1043
00:44:49,280 --> 00:44:49,760
 Why?

1044
00:44:49,760 --> 00:44:51,520
 Because it's going to give you a sense of,

1045
00:44:51,520 --> 00:44:54,360
 I'm in the season now, and that season's going to end,

1046
00:44:54,360 --> 00:44:55,960
 and the next season's going to come.

1047
00:44:55,960 --> 00:44:59,360
 Because life is ultimately like three acts.

1048
00:44:59,360 --> 00:45:01,040
 You're building a container, choosing

1049
00:45:01,040 --> 00:45:02,880
 to fill that container, then needing

1050
00:45:02,880 --> 00:45:05,760
 to give that container and its contents away.

1051
00:45:05,760 --> 00:45:08,720
 So that the three acts of life, I think,

1052
00:45:08,720 --> 00:45:13,400
 are many times behind the scenes when we feel despair.

1053
00:45:13,400 --> 00:45:16,040
 It's because we didn't properly recognize and prepare

1054
00:45:16,040 --> 00:45:18,360
 for the season that snuck up on us.

1055
00:45:18,360 --> 00:45:20,160
 But it's not like it wasn't coming for me.

1056
00:45:20,160 --> 00:45:23,160
 Well, it's not like midlife wasn't subtly there,

1057
00:45:23,160 --> 00:45:25,640
 showing, what is the gray hair?

1058
00:45:25,640 --> 00:45:27,000
 What's going on with that?

1059
00:45:27,000 --> 00:45:28,600
 Oh, the crow's feet, interesting.

1060
00:45:28,600 --> 00:45:29,920
 What could that mean?

1061
00:45:29,920 --> 00:45:31,640
 No, it was always coming.

1062
00:45:31,640 --> 00:45:33,280
 And yet, sometimes we act all surprised

1063
00:45:33,280 --> 00:45:35,960
 when something that was always going to come to an end

1064
00:45:35,960 --> 00:45:37,000
 all of a sudden comes.

1065
00:45:37,000 --> 00:45:38,400
 So how do we fight against that?

1066
00:45:38,400 --> 00:45:41,120
 We understand not just the season we're in today,

1067
00:45:41,120 --> 00:45:43,720
 but also the season that is coming.

1068
00:45:43,720 --> 00:45:47,080
 Proverbs 20, verse 29 says, "The glory of young men

1069
00:45:47,080 --> 00:45:50,360
 is their strength, and the splendor--"

1070
00:45:50,360 --> 00:45:51,960
 do you see that word, "splendor"?

1071
00:45:51,960 --> 00:45:53,600
 Does that sound awful?

1072
00:45:53,600 --> 00:45:56,940
 The Bible is honoring and recognizing.

1073
00:45:56,940 --> 00:45:59,160
 "Splendor" to what?

1074
00:45:59,160 --> 00:46:02,560
 The gray head of the old man.

1075
00:46:02,560 --> 00:46:04,320
 God really encouraged me with that verse

1076
00:46:04,320 --> 00:46:06,480
 one day when I said to Him, I'm not

1077
00:46:06,480 --> 00:46:10,560
 going to be terrified of what you've declared splendid.

1078
00:46:10,560 --> 00:46:11,880
 Do you hear me?

1079
00:46:11,880 --> 00:46:16,240
 I can have excitement for not just the current season

1080
00:46:16,240 --> 00:46:18,280
 that I want to hold on to, like forever 21,

1081
00:46:18,280 --> 00:46:20,040
 like what a life in this pit of hell,

1082
00:46:20,040 --> 00:46:23,000
 as though that were possible or desirable, right?

1083
00:46:23,000 --> 00:46:25,720
 But instead, to be excited about what God has already declared,

1084
00:46:25,720 --> 00:46:27,380
 not just glorious, which is what's now,

1085
00:46:27,380 --> 00:46:30,240
 but splendid, which is what's coming ahead.

1086
00:46:30,240 --> 00:46:32,520
 So we can understand what we're in,

1087
00:46:32,520 --> 00:46:34,680
 but also prepare for what season is coming next,

1088
00:46:34,680 --> 00:46:37,800
 so that it's not some big enemy that shows up.

1089
00:46:37,800 --> 00:46:39,680
 It's something we were preparing for.

1090
00:46:39,680 --> 00:46:41,040
 That's what Proverbs 6 says.

1091
00:46:41,040 --> 00:46:42,560
 Look at the ant, see how wise it is.

1092
00:46:42,560 --> 00:46:44,200
 It knows what season it's in today

1093
00:46:44,200 --> 00:46:45,400
 and the season that's coming.

1094
00:46:45,400 --> 00:46:47,040
 One little thing you could do would

1095
00:46:47,040 --> 00:46:49,160
 be to prepare your last will and testament.

1096
00:46:49,160 --> 00:46:51,700
 Did you know that almost 70% of Americans

1097
00:46:51,700 --> 00:46:53,960
 do not have an up-to-date will?

1098
00:46:53,960 --> 00:46:56,420
 And do you know what percent of Americans are going to die?

1099
00:46:56,420 --> 00:46:58,320
 All of them.

1100
00:46:58,320 --> 00:47:02,800
 So even just a simple act of honoring God by the way

1101
00:47:02,800 --> 00:47:05,200
 you're a steward over whatever you do--

1102
00:47:05,200 --> 00:47:06,160
 I don't have anything.

1103
00:47:06,160 --> 00:47:07,360
 I'm not going to be-- well, you'll

1104
00:47:07,360 --> 00:47:09,120
 be a steward over very little as long as you

1105
00:47:09,120 --> 00:47:10,920
 continue to have that attitude.

1106
00:47:10,920 --> 00:47:14,020
 It was the one talent person who hit us in the ground.

1107
00:47:14,020 --> 00:47:16,200
 So if you'll begin to say, whatever you give me, God,

1108
00:47:16,200 --> 00:47:20,760
 I'm going to honor you with how I am faithful to you with it,

1109
00:47:20,760 --> 00:47:22,560
 knowing I'm going to, at one point in my life,

1110
00:47:22,560 --> 00:47:24,560
 release all of it to you forever,

1111
00:47:24,560 --> 00:47:26,060
 and I'm going to prepare to do that.

1112
00:47:26,060 --> 00:47:31,240
 I actually think that tithing is a dress rehearsal for death

1113
00:47:31,240 --> 00:47:34,600
 that we get to be a part of every single week.

1114
00:47:34,600 --> 00:47:36,120
 Opening the hand, opening the hand.

1115
00:47:36,120 --> 00:47:38,240
 Because when you die, it's all coming out,

1116
00:47:38,240 --> 00:47:39,440
 whether you like it or not.

1117
00:47:39,440 --> 00:47:41,680
 So every time we open that hand up to God,

1118
00:47:41,680 --> 00:47:44,560
 it's a dress rehearsal for what is inevitable,

1119
00:47:44,560 --> 00:47:47,120
 and that is the release of everything back to him.

1120
00:47:47,120 --> 00:47:48,920
 So that's number one.

1121
00:47:48,920 --> 00:47:51,520
 Number two, jot this down, we connect the dots.

1122
00:47:51,520 --> 00:47:54,080
 If you're spiraling today, connect the dots.

1123
00:47:54,080 --> 00:47:57,820
 For me, there was not just during that 18-month-long

1124
00:47:57,820 --> 00:48:02,160
 period the question of, why is this happening?

1125
00:48:02,160 --> 00:48:03,440
 Oh, it's because I'm at midlife.

1126
00:48:03,440 --> 00:48:08,640
 There was also some other biological things going on.

1127
00:48:08,640 --> 00:48:10,200
 Pace of life stuff.

1128
00:48:10,200 --> 00:48:12,720
 Because the Bible says we are not just body.

1129
00:48:12,720 --> 00:48:13,920
 We're body, soul, spirit.

1130
00:48:13,920 --> 00:48:16,000
 In the church, we love to focus just on the spirit,

1131
00:48:16,000 --> 00:48:19,360
 but there was some other stuff going on there.

1132
00:48:19,360 --> 00:48:22,400
 How many things I was saying yes to, how hard I was going,

1133
00:48:22,400 --> 00:48:24,400
 the fact that I had been trying to basically burn

1134
00:48:24,400 --> 00:48:26,600
 the candle at both ends and in the middle

1135
00:48:26,600 --> 00:48:30,840
 for two decades in ministry, using language like,

1136
00:48:30,840 --> 00:48:33,240
 I'm going to drive the devil out of the state of Montana,

1137
00:48:33,240 --> 00:48:36,280
 just all this stupid stuff you say when you get a full tank

1138
00:48:36,280 --> 00:48:39,880
 of gas, and it's like, well, do we have to do all of Montana?

1139
00:48:39,880 --> 00:48:42,840
 So you get a little older, like, can we just do the county?

1140
00:48:42,840 --> 00:48:45,680
 You know what I'm saying?

1141
00:48:45,680 --> 00:48:47,840
 I'm being a little tongue-in-cheek and facetious

1142
00:48:47,840 --> 00:48:53,120
 here, but I think just the reality of hard living

1143
00:48:53,120 --> 00:48:56,520
 without always respecting my own personal limitations

1144
00:48:56,520 --> 00:49:00,240
 and the need to restore my own soul that I had to address.

1145
00:49:00,240 --> 00:49:03,120
 The fact that I would have, for a long season of my life,

1146
00:49:03,120 --> 00:49:05,880
 found it completely crazy to think of giving myself

1147
00:49:05,880 --> 00:49:07,960
 a day to go hiking, or a day to go fly fishing,

1148
00:49:07,960 --> 00:49:10,080
 or a day to play tennis, to go sit in the sauna

1149
00:49:10,080 --> 00:49:12,440
 and not feel guilty, because there was surely

1150
00:49:12,440 --> 00:49:15,640
 something I could be doing for God in that moment.

1151
00:49:15,640 --> 00:49:20,000
 And so learning some of those rhythms of rest, and release,

1152
00:49:20,000 --> 00:49:24,120
 and Selah, and Sabbath.

1153
00:49:24,120 --> 00:49:26,880
 So connecting the dots on, that's how I got here.

1154
00:49:26,880 --> 00:49:28,760
 I got here because the body does keep score.

1155
00:49:28,760 --> 00:49:31,040
 I got here because pace does matter.

1156
00:49:31,040 --> 00:49:35,480
 And I'm a simple human, not Iron Man, right?

1157
00:49:35,480 --> 00:49:39,080
 Just that realization that I have limitations.

1158
00:49:39,080 --> 00:49:40,600
 I also had to get off pre-workout.

1159
00:49:40,600 --> 00:49:42,600
 I don't know if this could be for somebody here,

1160
00:49:42,600 --> 00:49:44,640
 but my doctor was like, hey, could you

1161
00:49:44,640 --> 00:49:46,760
 text me a picture of everything you take in a day?

1162
00:49:46,760 --> 00:49:49,240
 And I texted the pre-workout to her, and she wrote back,

1163
00:49:49,240 --> 00:49:50,960
 have you read this?

1164
00:49:50,960 --> 00:49:52,000
 Have you ever read this?

1165
00:49:52,000 --> 00:49:54,720
 It says may cause feelings of panic, you moron.

1166
00:49:54,720 --> 00:49:55,640
 She didn't say that.

1167
00:49:55,640 --> 00:49:56,640
 Doctors don't say moron.

1168
00:49:56,640 --> 00:49:58,200
 I said that.

1169
00:49:58,200 --> 00:50:00,240
 I did that all myself.

1170
00:50:00,240 --> 00:50:02,160
 I'm like, Lord, help me with my panic attacks.

1171
00:50:02,160 --> 00:50:02,920
 Glug, glug, glug.

1172
00:50:02,920 --> 00:50:06,680
 You know, it's like--

1173
00:50:06,680 --> 00:50:07,920
 it could be as simple as that.

1174
00:50:07,920 --> 00:50:08,600
 You're like, pray for me.

1175
00:50:08,600 --> 00:50:09,460
 I have headaches every day.

1176
00:50:09,460 --> 00:50:10,800
 Tell me what you drink in a day.

1177
00:50:10,800 --> 00:50:11,720
 Nothing but sweet tea.

1178
00:50:11,720 --> 00:50:16,720
 Connect the dots.

1179
00:50:16,720 --> 00:50:19,600
 I had family of origin stuff too.

1180
00:50:19,600 --> 00:50:23,320
 I had to deal with a lot of stuff from my childhood

1181
00:50:23,320 --> 00:50:26,800
 I had never faced down.

1182
00:50:26,800 --> 00:50:27,960
 It was all connected.

1183
00:50:27,960 --> 00:50:32,520
 OK, number three, recalibrate your scoreboard.

1184
00:50:32,520 --> 00:50:34,440
 This was huge for me in my second half of life.

1185
00:50:34,440 --> 00:50:36,200
 I was talking to a friend this morning playing tennis,

1186
00:50:36,200 --> 00:50:38,640
 and he asked about what's getting me so much joy

1187
00:50:38,640 --> 00:50:39,600
 in ministry these days.

1188
00:50:39,600 --> 00:50:41,240
 And I was saying, it has everything

1189
00:50:41,240 --> 00:50:43,840
 to do with the chance to fight for young people

1190
00:50:43,840 --> 00:50:47,040
 and everything to do with to fight for other leaders who

1191
00:50:47,040 --> 00:50:48,880
 are going to release and reach young people.

1192
00:50:48,880 --> 00:50:51,320
 And that's what puts bright, shining light in my eyes,

1193
00:50:51,320 --> 00:50:54,840
 much more than is it the biggest thing or the most--

1194
00:50:54,840 --> 00:50:57,040
 all that stuff is fantastic, right?

1195
00:50:57,040 --> 00:50:58,580
 I want to reach everyone for Christ.

1196
00:50:58,580 --> 00:50:59,080
 Amazing.

1197
00:50:59,080 --> 00:50:59,920
 We get it, right?

1198
00:50:59,920 --> 00:51:00,720
 That's fantastic.

1199
00:51:00,720 --> 00:51:03,720
 But I've recalibrated my scoreboard

1200
00:51:03,720 --> 00:51:06,960
 to not just what appears successful,

1201
00:51:06,960 --> 00:51:09,480
 but what is actually significant connected

1202
00:51:09,480 --> 00:51:12,320
 to what God has called for me to participate

1203
00:51:12,320 --> 00:51:15,680
 in in the second half of my life.

1204
00:51:15,680 --> 00:51:17,560
 And a part of that is just, for me,

1205
00:51:17,560 --> 00:51:22,280
 reigniting the flame of passion for personal evangelism,

1206
00:51:22,280 --> 00:51:25,800
 not from a platform, but just person to person and heart

1207
00:51:25,800 --> 00:51:29,920
 to heart, and finding a column on your scoreboard

1208
00:51:29,920 --> 00:51:33,280
 for things that no one on Earth is going to celebrate,

1209
00:51:33,280 --> 00:51:36,000
 but ignites the greatest applause in heaven

1210
00:51:36,000 --> 00:51:38,560
 because God sees it's what He has for you

1211
00:51:38,560 --> 00:51:42,280
 in this coming season of recalibration and retooling

1212
00:51:42,280 --> 00:51:44,320
 of the factory of your heart.

1213
00:51:44,320 --> 00:51:45,640
 I mean, don't get me wrong.

1214
00:51:45,640 --> 00:51:47,120
 Luke Skywalker's great.

1215
00:51:47,120 --> 00:51:49,800
 We all want to be Luke Skywalker and Leia and Han Solo.

1216
00:51:49,800 --> 00:51:52,600
 But man, the kingdom of God needs some Obi-Wan Kenobis

1217
00:51:52,600 --> 00:51:56,000
 and some Yodas as well, right?

1218
00:51:56,000 --> 00:51:58,400
 And maybe even Jar Jar Binks, although that's debatable.

1219
00:51:58,400 --> 00:52:00,000
 We could go back and forth about that.

1220
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:01,320
 Hot take, he's the worst.

1221
00:52:01,320 --> 00:52:05,360
 OK, anyhow, number four, I would say this.

1222
00:52:05,360 --> 00:52:07,600
 If you're spiraling today, be kind.

1223
00:52:07,600 --> 00:52:08,960
 You've never been here before.

1224
00:52:08,960 --> 00:52:13,640
 Be kind.

1225
00:52:13,640 --> 00:52:15,520
 You've never been here before.

1226
00:52:15,520 --> 00:52:20,240
 If I'm completely honest, I made my season of spiraling worse

1227
00:52:20,240 --> 00:52:24,440
 because I was berating myself for not doing better.

1228
00:52:24,440 --> 00:52:28,880
 And very few things will make you feel less better when

1229
00:52:28,880 --> 00:52:30,680
 you're feeling bad than you trying

1230
00:52:30,680 --> 00:52:35,320
 to make yourself feeling bad for not feeling better.

1231
00:52:35,320 --> 00:52:36,920
 And when God opened my eyes to this,

1232
00:52:36,920 --> 00:52:38,680
 I was doing a hospital visit.

1233
00:52:38,680 --> 00:52:41,280
 My friend, Stu, he's been a part of our church for--

1234
00:52:41,280 --> 00:52:44,800
 well, he had been a part of our church for 18 years.

1235
00:52:44,800 --> 00:52:47,000
 And he had Parkinson's.

1236
00:52:47,000 --> 00:52:49,360
 And his wife called me and said, Stu thinks he's dying.

1237
00:52:49,360 --> 00:52:50,360
 Can you get here as quick as you could?

1238
00:52:50,360 --> 00:52:52,120
 And the quickest I could get there was the next morning.

1239
00:52:52,120 --> 00:52:56,080
 So I walked into his room, and he was skin and bones.

1240
00:52:56,080 --> 00:52:58,400
 And he was-- you know what he was?

1241
00:52:58,400 --> 00:53:00,160
 He was so ashamed.

1242
00:53:00,160 --> 00:53:02,840
 He said, I can't believe I asked her to call you.

1243
00:53:02,840 --> 00:53:04,680
 I thought I was dying last night.

1244
00:53:04,680 --> 00:53:05,720
 I didn't even die.

1245
00:53:05,720 --> 00:53:08,880
 I actually feel really good this morning.

1246
00:53:08,880 --> 00:53:11,480
 He was embarrassed, and I laughed.

1247
00:53:11,480 --> 00:53:12,880
 And you know what I said to Stu?

1248
00:53:12,880 --> 00:53:14,000
 We had a good relationship.

1249
00:53:14,000 --> 00:53:16,680
 I said, Stu, you're terrible at this.

1250
00:53:16,680 --> 00:53:20,160
 You're so bad at dying.

1251
00:53:20,160 --> 00:53:23,440
 And then I said, but how could you be good at it?

1252
00:53:23,440 --> 00:53:27,280
 You've never done it before.

1253
00:53:27,280 --> 00:53:29,120
 And he laughed.

1254
00:53:29,120 --> 00:53:31,440
 And I said, I have a prediction, Stu.

1255
00:53:31,440 --> 00:53:34,680
 I said, I bet you're going to suck at dying when you die.

1256
00:53:34,680 --> 00:53:36,040
 You're going to be so bad at it.

1257
00:53:36,040 --> 00:53:37,360
 It's going to be so clumsy.

1258
00:53:37,360 --> 00:53:40,280
 It's not going to be, like, finesse.

1259
00:53:40,280 --> 00:53:43,520
 It's going to be like, ah, eh.

1260
00:53:43,520 --> 00:53:46,520
 That's what I said.

1261
00:53:46,520 --> 00:53:50,480
 I'm not a great pastor, obviously.

1262
00:53:50,480 --> 00:53:54,400
 I said, you're going to be so bad at dying because you've

1263
00:53:54,400 --> 00:53:56,320
 never done it before.

1264
00:53:56,320 --> 00:53:59,200
 I said, but do you know who's so good at death?

1265
00:53:59,200 --> 00:54:00,960
 Jesus.

1266
00:54:00,960 --> 00:54:05,000
 He has never dropped the ball on the death of one of his saints

1267
00:54:05,000 --> 00:54:05,960
 ever.

1268
00:54:05,960 --> 00:54:07,480
 He conquered death, and he's going

1269
00:54:07,480 --> 00:54:10,760
 to bring you through despite you being bad at it.

1270
00:54:10,760 --> 00:54:12,680
 So you can trust your death to him.

1271
00:54:12,680 --> 00:54:13,640
 And Stu laughed.

1272
00:54:13,640 --> 00:54:15,400
 He laid his head back on the pillow.

1273
00:54:15,400 --> 00:54:16,200
 He closed his eyes.

1274
00:54:16,200 --> 00:54:17,560
 And it was just a few days later,

1275
00:54:17,560 --> 00:54:24,080
 he went home to be with Jesus, badly, clumsily.

1276
00:54:24,080 --> 00:54:26,720
 But Jesus guided him through.

1277
00:54:26,720 --> 00:54:29,200
 How could you be good at what you're

1278
00:54:29,200 --> 00:54:31,160
 dealing with today, loved one?

1279
00:54:31,160 --> 00:54:32,920
 You've never been here before.

1280
00:54:32,920 --> 00:54:34,000
 You've never been 25.

1281
00:54:34,000 --> 00:54:35,620
 You've never started a company before.

1282
00:54:35,620 --> 00:54:36,880
 You've never had to sell the company.

1283
00:54:36,880 --> 00:54:38,200
 You've never been at Empty Nest.

1284
00:54:38,200 --> 00:54:39,640
 You've never been here.

1285
00:54:39,640 --> 00:54:41,960
 Of course, you're not good at it.

1286
00:54:41,960 --> 00:54:43,600
 So quit trying to act like you're

1287
00:54:43,600 --> 00:54:45,760
 good at what you've never done before and just tell

1288
00:54:45,760 --> 00:54:49,320
 your father you are bad at it and let him help you,

1289
00:54:49,320 --> 00:54:50,760
 because he's good.

1290
00:54:50,760 --> 00:54:56,160
 All the time, God is good.

1291
00:54:56,160 --> 00:54:58,880
 So be kind to yourself.

1292
00:54:58,880 --> 00:55:00,120
 You've never been here before.

1293
00:55:00,120 --> 00:55:02,000
 And then lastly, we close with this.

1294
00:55:02,000 --> 00:55:03,560
 And this is so important.

1295
00:55:03,560 --> 00:55:07,520
 Anchor your identity in what can't be taken away.

1296
00:55:07,520 --> 00:55:13,120
 Anchor your identity in what can't be taken away.

1297
00:55:13,120 --> 00:55:16,080
 To be just completely and totally in a moment

1298
00:55:16,080 --> 00:55:19,880
 of transparent confession before you,

1299
00:55:19,880 --> 00:55:25,720
 there was a lot of my identity in that season

1300
00:55:25,720 --> 00:55:29,160
 I discovered, thanks to the kindness of the Holy Spirit,

1301
00:55:29,160 --> 00:55:31,080
 that came from what I do for God.

1302
00:55:31,080 --> 00:55:37,040
 Because I planted a church at 23,

1303
00:55:37,040 --> 00:55:38,680
 wrote my first book at 30.

1304
00:55:38,680 --> 00:55:40,680
 I started preaching at 14.

1305
00:55:40,680 --> 00:55:43,640
 My whole life, I was always being celebrated

1306
00:55:43,640 --> 00:55:46,200
 as this young man doing great things for God.

1307
00:55:46,200 --> 00:55:50,240
 And I never intended for that to be what I built me on.

1308
00:55:50,240 --> 00:55:54,720
 But there was some part of that that got cooked in there,

1309
00:55:54,720 --> 00:55:59,720
 that God was trying to burn out and smoke out.

1310
00:55:59,720 --> 00:56:00,800
 Because here's the thing.

1311
00:56:00,800 --> 00:56:03,880
 There is going to come a day when my body is going to slow.

1312
00:56:03,880 --> 00:56:06,200
 And I will not be able to hop on an airplane and preach.

1313
00:56:06,200 --> 00:56:08,080
 And I will not have anything to say in a book

1314
00:56:08,080 --> 00:56:09,920
 that anyone's going to want to read.

1315
00:56:09,920 --> 00:56:13,520
 There is going to come a day when I won't be doing anything

1316
00:56:13,520 --> 00:56:16,440
 for the kingdom of God, drooling down

1317
00:56:16,440 --> 00:56:19,600
 my shirt in a retirement home, or in a roadside

1318
00:56:19,600 --> 00:56:20,840
 ditch after a car accident.

1319
00:56:20,840 --> 00:56:24,920
 My identity in that moment, it will--

1320
00:56:24,920 --> 00:56:28,720
 if it's based on anything that's me, let me tell you something.

1321
00:56:28,720 --> 00:56:30,960
 That ship will have sailed.

1322
00:56:30,960 --> 00:56:35,360
 And it's coming for us all in the things of this world

1323
00:56:35,360 --> 00:56:39,280
 that we would be tempted to build our identity from and on.

1324
00:56:39,280 --> 00:56:41,920
 But do you know what will never be taken from you?

1325
00:56:41,920 --> 00:56:47,960
 That you are a blood son or daughter of the King of kings.

1326
00:56:47,960 --> 00:56:49,880
 What never will be taken from me is

1327
00:56:49,880 --> 00:56:52,240
 that I was created in God's image, that He loves me,

1328
00:56:52,240 --> 00:56:53,680
 that He sees me, that He knows me,

1329
00:56:53,680 --> 00:56:55,980
 that He's got my name written on the palm of His hands.

1330
00:56:55,980 --> 00:56:58,320
 And so my season of spiraling, it

1331
00:56:58,320 --> 00:57:00,680
 was there to get me to recalibrate

1332
00:57:00,680 --> 00:57:02,320
 what actually matters.

1333
00:57:02,320 --> 00:57:04,280
 And that is that Jesus loves me.

1334
00:57:04,280 --> 00:57:05,720
 And that's enough.

1335
00:57:05,720 --> 00:57:10,600
 And that none of what I do for God is anything other than just

1336
00:57:10,600 --> 00:57:13,480
 thank you that you gave me that opportunity and back

1337
00:57:13,480 --> 00:57:17,080
 to the serious business of being lost in your presence,

1338
00:57:17,080 --> 00:57:18,320
 of being lost in your love.

1339
00:57:18,320 --> 00:57:25,000
 The weekend I finished writing the book that

1340
00:57:25,000 --> 00:57:28,160
 has the message in it I'm sharing with you,

1341
00:57:28,160 --> 00:57:31,960
 18 months of spiraling, then the next several years

1342
00:57:31,960 --> 00:57:34,280
 of condensing and catalyzing those lessons in your book

1343
00:57:34,280 --> 00:57:36,320
 form, the very weekend I finished

1344
00:57:36,320 --> 00:57:38,600
 writing that book, The Rough Draft,

1345
00:57:38,600 --> 00:57:41,880
 I called my dad to tell him about it.

1346
00:57:41,880 --> 00:57:43,480
 Called my dad every day.

1347
00:57:43,480 --> 00:57:45,000
 Talked to him every day.

1348
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:46,680
 He was my best man at my wedding.

1349
00:57:46,680 --> 00:57:47,720
 He was my best friend.

1350
00:57:47,720 --> 00:57:50,880
 He was a champion to me.

1351
00:57:50,880 --> 00:57:53,640
 In the very same week I finished this book,

1352
00:57:53,640 --> 00:57:56,000
 Blessed Are the Spiraling, my dad

1353
00:57:56,000 --> 00:57:58,400
 called me to tell me he had been diagnosed with stage 4

1354
00:57:58,400 --> 00:58:01,040
 pancreatic cancer.

1355
00:58:01,040 --> 00:58:03,720
 And one year to the day of his diagnosis,

1356
00:58:03,720 --> 00:58:08,440
 my dad, skin and bones, he struggled

1357
00:58:08,440 --> 00:58:12,040
 to say his last words before he went home to be with Christ.

1358
00:58:12,040 --> 00:58:14,320
 He got to go with me to the last Passion Conference

1359
00:58:14,320 --> 00:58:18,040
 in the Mercedes-Benz Arena when Agnes Day broke out.

1360
00:58:18,040 --> 00:58:19,760
 And we all sang about the holiness of God

1361
00:58:19,760 --> 00:58:22,360
 for 17 minutes or something like that.

1362
00:58:22,360 --> 00:58:24,400
 He was there in the room when it happened.

1363
00:58:24,400 --> 00:58:26,800
 He was so sick with chemotherapy.

1364
00:58:26,800 --> 00:58:29,320
 And the cancer was eating his lungs and his liver

1365
00:58:29,320 --> 00:58:30,280
 and his pancreas.

1366
00:58:30,280 --> 00:58:34,800
 And he was freezing and had his hoodie on.

1367
00:58:34,800 --> 00:58:37,640
 And my dad was dying.

1368
00:58:37,640 --> 00:58:43,840
 On his deathbed, he spoke one last time.

1369
00:58:43,840 --> 00:58:46,680
 He did it three times.

1370
00:58:46,680 --> 00:58:49,480
 He would open his eyes and his hand would open and close

1371
00:58:49,480 --> 00:58:50,280
 and open and close.

1372
00:58:50,280 --> 00:58:59,920
 And he would say over and over again, wow, wow, wow.

1373
00:59:01,280 --> 00:59:05,680
 Wow, wow, wow.

1374
00:59:05,680 --> 00:59:15,200
 And I didn't know my dad, who taught me how to ride a bike,

1375
00:59:15,200 --> 00:59:17,240
 who gave me my first Bible, who taught me

1376
00:59:17,240 --> 00:59:20,720
 how to treat a woman with God's love and kindness,

1377
00:59:20,720 --> 00:59:22,760
 told me when you go on a date for the first time,

1378
00:59:22,760 --> 00:59:24,200
 you start that date with prayer.

1379
00:59:24,200 --> 00:59:28,520
 Invoke God's name, His presence in that car, in that date.

1380
00:59:28,520 --> 00:59:30,080
 I did it.

1381
00:59:30,080 --> 00:59:32,960
 My dad, who had taught me how to do so many things,

1382
00:59:32,960 --> 00:59:38,360
 how to drink my coffee black like a man does,

1383
00:59:38,360 --> 00:59:40,320
 always take the lid off because it tastes better

1384
00:59:40,320 --> 00:59:42,400
 with no lid on that coffee.

1385
00:59:42,400 --> 00:59:43,920
 He would spill his coffee everywhere.

1386
00:59:43,920 --> 00:59:46,080
 His car was filthy.

1387
00:59:46,080 --> 00:59:48,280
 Driving down the road like a psychopath

1388
00:59:48,280 --> 00:59:50,200
 with coffee spilling.

1389
00:59:50,200 --> 00:59:54,680
 My dad, who taught me all those things,

1390
00:59:54,680 --> 00:59:59,320
 was teaching me how to die.

1391
00:59:59,320 --> 01:00:03,440
 Wow, wow, wow.

1392
01:00:03,440 --> 01:00:11,360
 So no matter what pain you go through on this earth,

1393
01:00:11,360 --> 01:00:16,600
 just keep the actual prize in your mind.

1394
01:00:16,600 --> 01:00:18,640
 The end of your spiral staircase spiraling up,

1395
01:00:18,640 --> 01:00:21,280
 one shaky step at a time, at the end waiting for you

1396
01:00:21,280 --> 01:00:25,320
 is not something, but someone.

1397
01:00:25,320 --> 01:00:31,760
 His name is Jesus, and He always leads His children in triumph.

1398
01:00:31,760 --> 01:00:36,920
 And so Father, we thank you for being

1399
01:00:36,920 --> 01:00:39,080
 the author of Seasons of Spiraling,

1400
01:00:39,080 --> 01:00:42,920
 having written every word to the story to bring us back to you,

1401
01:00:42,920 --> 01:00:43,960
 to bring us back to you.

1402
01:00:43,960 --> 01:00:46,360
 If you're here and you would say in one of these moments,

1403
01:00:46,360 --> 01:00:48,320
 you would say, I'm spiraling today,

1404
01:00:48,320 --> 01:00:51,720
 but I choose to believe I'm spiraling up in Jesus' name.

1405
01:00:51,720 --> 01:00:53,640
 Could I just ask you to raise a hand up?

1406
01:00:53,640 --> 01:00:54,520
 Just raise your hand.

1407
01:00:54,520 --> 01:00:57,840
 Torch live every single heart, every single life.

1408
01:00:57,840 --> 01:00:58,640
 Thank you, Jesus.

1409
01:00:58,640 --> 01:00:59,160
 Thank you.

1410
01:00:59,160 --> 01:01:00,640
 Touch my friends.

1411
01:01:00,640 --> 01:01:01,400
 Give them courage.

1412
01:01:01,400 --> 01:01:03,000
 Give them peace.

1413
01:01:03,000 --> 01:01:05,720
 Thank you for the confession with eyes closed, hands up.

1414
01:01:05,720 --> 01:01:07,400
 But I pray for grace in a moment

1415
01:01:07,400 --> 01:01:09,920
 to ask for prayer from someone in their life

1416
01:01:09,920 --> 01:01:14,080
 to pray for them and give them love and show them courage.

1417
01:01:14,080 --> 01:01:15,040
 Bless your people now.

1418
01:01:15,040 --> 01:01:16,480
 You put your hands down.

1419
01:01:16,480 --> 01:01:18,360
 If you're here and you've not trusted Christ

1420
01:01:18,360 --> 01:01:21,320
 and you need to be saved, your works, your goodness,

1421
01:01:21,320 --> 01:01:23,520
 your being kind can't save you.

1422
01:01:23,520 --> 01:01:26,720
 Only the blood of Jesus shed for you on the cross,

1423
01:01:26,720 --> 01:01:30,680
 his resurrection, his life in you can save you

1424
01:01:30,680 --> 01:01:33,280
 from your sins, can give you that promise of heaven,

1425
01:01:33,280 --> 01:01:35,680
 can give you all those three things Jonathan Edwards talked

1426
01:01:35,680 --> 01:01:37,160
 about and more.

1427
01:01:37,160 --> 01:01:39,080
 If you're here and you've never trusted Christ,

1428
01:01:39,080 --> 01:01:40,720
 I'm going to pray a prayer.

1429
01:01:40,720 --> 01:01:42,080
 I want you to pray it with me.

1430
01:01:42,080 --> 01:01:45,320
 This is a prayer I prayed at 14 to give my life to Jesus.

1431
01:01:45,320 --> 01:01:46,920
 This can be your prayer tonight to God

1432
01:01:46,920 --> 01:01:49,480
 if God's brought you into this moment for such a time as this

1433
01:01:49,480 --> 01:01:52,360
 to save you in his kindness, secure you

1434
01:01:52,360 --> 01:01:53,920
 forever because of his love.

1435
01:01:53,920 --> 01:01:56,200
 I want you to pray this prayer with me.

1436
01:01:56,200 --> 01:01:58,160
 For the benefit of those praying,

1437
01:01:58,160 --> 01:02:00,760
 we as the church family are going to pray this out loud

1438
01:02:00,760 --> 01:02:03,040
 together with you to show we're with you,

1439
01:02:03,040 --> 01:02:04,600
 proud to be with you in this decision.

1440
01:02:04,600 --> 01:02:06,000
 Pray this prayer out loud.

1441
01:02:06,000 --> 01:02:06,920
 Mean it in your heart.

1442
01:02:06,920 --> 01:02:07,680
 God will hear you.

1443
01:02:07,680 --> 01:02:09,260
 Church family, let's pray it together.

1444
01:02:09,260 --> 01:02:12,840
 Dear God, I know I'm a sinner.

1445
01:02:12,840 --> 01:02:15,760
 I can't fix myself.

1446
01:02:15,760 --> 01:02:22,720
 But I believe you can because of Jesus, because of the cross.

1447
01:02:22,720 --> 01:02:24,680
 I repent.

1448
01:02:24,680 --> 01:02:26,960
 Ask you to forgive me.

1449
01:02:26,960 --> 01:02:29,160
 Thank you for the cross.

1450
01:02:29,160 --> 01:02:31,720
 Thank you for the resurrection.

1451
01:02:31,720 --> 01:02:40,400
 Make my heart your home, my song your throne.

1452
01:02:40,400 --> 01:02:41,400
 In Jesus' name.

1453
01:02:45,680 --> 01:02:46,520
 Amen.

